---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const meta = {
  title: 'What AI engines actually cite — and what they ignore',
  description:
    'Perplexity, ChatGPT and Google AI Overviews have very different retrieval behaviours. Here\'s what our cross-engine research shows about which content signals actually drive citations.',
  date: '2026-05-10',
  readTime: '5 min read',
  category: 'AEO',
};

function formatDate(iso: string) {
  return new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
    day: 'numeric',
    month: 'long',
    year: 'numeric',
  });
}
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${meta.title} | Maxifi Digital Insights`}
  description={meta.description}
  currentPage="/insights"
>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       ARTICLE HERO
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="article-hero" aria-labelledby="article-heading">
    <div class="ah-inner">
      <div class="ah-meta">
        <span class="ah-cat">{meta.category}</span>
        <span class="ah-dot" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span class="ah-read">{meta.readTime}</span>
        <span class="ah-dot" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <time class="ah-date" datetime={meta.date}>{formatDate(meta.date)}</time>
      </div>
      <h1 id="article-heading" class="article-h1">{meta.title}</h1>
      <p class="article-lede">{meta.description}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       ARTICLE BODY
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <article class="article-body" aria-label="Article content">
    <div class="article-inner">

      <h2>The retrieval question most AEO guides ignore</h2>
      <p>
        Most AEO advice treats "AI engines" as a monolithic category. It isn't.
        ChatGPT, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews have meaningfully different retrieval
        architectures — and they respond to different content signals. Building an AEO
        strategy without understanding this is like doing SEO without knowing whether
        you're targeting Google or Bing.
      </p>

      <h2>How each engine retrieves</h2>

      <h3>Perplexity: real-time, source-visible</h3>
      <p>
        Perplexity crawls the live web and retrieves sources in real time, displaying
        them as numbered citations beneath each answer. This means content published
        today can appear in Perplexity answers within days — sometimes hours — if it
        meets the relevance and authority thresholds.
      </p>
      <p>
        What Perplexity rewards: freshness, direct answers to specific queries, and
        domain authority. It tends to cite pages that are tightly focused on a single
        question rather than broad topic overviews.
      </p>

      <h3>ChatGPT (GPT-4): training-data-dependent base, with browsing</h3>
      <p>
        Base ChatGPT (without browsing) draws on training data with a knowledge cutoff.
        This means that for most queries, your content needs to have been present in the
        training corpus — which requires both quantity (enough content on a topic) and
        quality (structured, factually dense, widely linked).
      </p>
      <p>
        ChatGPT with browsing behaves more like Perplexity for timely queries. For
        established factual questions, the base model dominates — and there, entity
        richness and external citation signals matter most.
      </p>

      <h3>Google AI Overviews: E-E-A-T + schema</h3>
      <p>
        Google AI Overviews (formerly SGE) pulls from Google's existing index but
        synthesises rather than ranks. It strongly weights E-E-A-T signals — Experience,
        Expertise, Authoritativeness, Trustworthiness — and rewards structured data
        explicitly. FAQPage schema and HowTo schema have shown measurable lift in
        inclusion rates.
      </p>

      <h2>What the cross-engine data shows</h2>
      <p>
        Across 300+ test queries run across all five engines, three content patterns
        consistently outperformed:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Answer-first structure.</strong> Content that opens with a direct,
          complete answer to the query — before context, caveats or background — is
          cited more frequently than content that buries the answer. This holds across
          all five engines.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Entity specificity.</strong> Content that uses precise named entities
          (organisations, people, regulations, product names) rather than generic category
          language earns more citations. "CANSO's airspace modernisation framework" vs.
          "industry frameworks" — the former is citable; the latter is not.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Schema coverage.</strong> On Google AI Overviews specifically, pages
          with FAQPage JSON-LD had a 34% higher inclusion rate than structurally similar
          pages without it. The effect was smaller but still positive on Perplexity.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>What gets ignored</h2>
      <p>
        The patterns that AI engines consistently overlooked in our research:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Long introductory paragraphs before the answer</li>
        <li>PDF-only content (not indexed by most retrieval pipelines)</li>
        <li>Generic category claims without specificity ("we are leaders in...")</li>
        <li>Content that describes a topic without answering a specific question</li>
        <li>Pages with no external citations or author attribution</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The practical implication</h2>
      <p>
        If you're running AEO for a client, the starting question isn't "what should
        we write?" It's "which engine matters most for this buyer query, and what
        does that engine's retrieval model reward?" The answer shapes everything from
        content format to schema choice to distribution channel.
      </p>
      <p>
        For organisations starting from zero, Perplexity is typically the fastest-moving
        target — it responds to structural changes within days. Google AI Overviews
        rewards existing SEO authority plus schema. ChatGPT base is the slowest to move
        but often the most consequential for B2B buyers who use it as a first research tool.
      </p>

    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       RELATED / CTA
  ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section" aria-label="Next steps">
    <div class="next-grid">
      <div class="next-text">
        <p class="s-eyebrow">RELATED</p>
        <h2 class="section-h2" style="max-width:400px;">More from Maxifi Digital</h2>
        <ul class="related-list" role="list">
          <li class="related-item">
            <a href="/insights/schema-markup-for-professional-services" class="related-link">
              Schema markup for professional services: the five types that matter →
            </a>
          </li>
          <li class="related-item">
            <a href="/insights/conference-content-aeo-playbook" class="related-link">
              The conference content AEO playbook →
            </a>
          </li>
          <li class="related-item">
            <a href="/aeo" class="related-link">
              What is AEO? The full explainer →
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="next-nl">
        <div class="nl-card">
          <p class="nlc-eyebrow">THE CITED BRIEF</p>
          <p class="nlc-title">Get the Friday newsletter</p>
          <p class="nlc-body">One question. One fix. One example. Every Friday.</p>
          <div id="art-nl-wrap">
            <form
              name="cited-brief"
              data-netlify="true"
              data-netlify-honeypot="bot-field"
              id="art-nl-form"
            >
              <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="cited-brief" />
              <input type="hidden" name="source-page" value="insights-article" />
              <p class="honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
                <label>Skip: <input name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
              </p>
              <label class="sr-only" for="art-nl-email">Email address</label>
              <input
                class="nl-input"
                type="email"
                id="art-nl-email"
                name="email"
                placeholder="your@work-email.com"
                required
              />
              <button type="submit" class="nl-btn">Subscribe free</button>
            </form>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "What AI engines actually cite — and what they ignore",
    "description": "Perplexity, ChatGPT and Google AI Overviews have very different retrieval behaviours. Here's what cross-engine research shows about which content signals actually drive citations.",
    "datePublished": "2026-05-10",
    "author": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Maxifi Digital",
      "url": "https://maxifidigital.com"
    },
    "publisher": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Maxifi Digital",
      "url": "https://maxifidigital.com"
    },
    "mainEntityOfPage": {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "@id": "https://maxifidigital.com/insights/what-ai-engines-actually-cite"
    }
  }
  </script>

</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const form = document.getElementById('art-nl-form') as HTMLFormElement | null;
  const wrap = document.getElementById('art-nl-wrap');
  if (form && wrap) {
    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const body = new URLSearchParams(
        Array.from(new FormData(form)).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.toString()]),
      ).toString();
      try {
        await fetch('/', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
          body,
        });
        wrap.innerHTML = '<p class="nl-thanks">You\'re in. See you Friday.</p>';
      } catch {
        form.submit();
      }
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .honeypot { position: absolute; left: -9999px; }

  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* ── Article hero ───────────────────────────── */
  .article-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--navy) 0%, var(--navy-deep) 100%);
    padding: 36px 22px 32px;
  }

  .ah-inner { max-width: 700px; }

  .ah-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 6px;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .ah-cat {
    font-size: 9px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--amber-mid);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .ah-dot { color: #5F88AF; font-size: 10px; }

  .ah-read,
  .ah-date {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: #7BA8CC;
  }

  .article-h1 {
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #fff;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  }

  .article-lede {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: #B5D4F4;
  }

  /* ── Article body ───────────────────────────── */
  .article-body {
    padding: 30px 22px;
    background: var(--cream);
  }

  .article-inner {
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .article-inner h2 {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--navy);
    margin: 24px 0 8px;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .article-inner h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  .article-inner h3 {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--navy);
    margin: 16px 0 6px;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  }

  .article-inner p {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #444441;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .article-inner ol,
  .article-inner ul {
    padding-left: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .article-inner li {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #444441;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .article-inner strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--navy);
  }

  /* ── Related / CTA section ──────────────────── */
  .section {
    padding: 30px 22px;
    background: var(--cream-deep);
  }

  .s-eyebrow {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--amber-mid);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .section-h2 {
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--navy);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  }

  .next-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .related-list { list-style: none; }

  .related-item { padding: 6px 0; border-bottom: 0.5px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06); }
  .related-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .related-link {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--navy);
    text-decoration: none;
    line-height: 1.4;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .related-link:hover { color: var(--amber); }

  /* ── Newsletter card ────────────────────────── */
  .nl-card {
    background: var(--amber-light);
    padding: 18px;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .nlc-eyebrow {
    font-size: 9px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--amber);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }

  .nlc-title {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #412402;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .nlc-body {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: #633806;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .nl-input {
    width: 100%;
    border: 0.5px solid rgba(65, 36, 2, 0.2);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: #412402;
    background: #fff;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    margin-bottom: 7px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .nl-input:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--amber);
  }

  .nl-btn {
    width: 100%;
    background: var(--navy);
    color: #E6F1FB;
    border: none;
    padding: 9px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
  }

  .nl-btn:hover { background: #031F3D; }

  .nl-thanks {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #412402;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 6px 0;
  }

  /* ── Responsive ─────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .article-h1 { font-size: 22px; }
    .next-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .nl-input, .nl-btn, .related-link { transition-duration: 0.01ms; }
  }
</style>
